    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Sequence Log-Probability"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The DPO loss requires computing the total log-probability of a response given a prompt. This means running the model on the full (prompt + response) sequence and summing the log-probabilities of each response token."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tokenize_sequence(text, vocab_size=256):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [min(t, vocab_size - 1) for t in list(text.encode(\"utf-8\"))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def compute_sequence_log_prob(model, prompt_tokens, response_tokens, max_seq_len=128):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    full_sequence = prompt_tokens + response_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if len(full_sequence) > max_seq_len:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        full_sequence = full_sequence[:max_seq_len]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if len(full_sequence) < 2:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    input_ids = np.array(full_sequence[:-1]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target_ids = np.array(full_sequence[1:])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    logits = model.forward(input_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    logits = logits[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_logits = logits.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log_probs = logits - max_logits - np.log("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        np.exp(logits - max_logits).sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prompt_len = len(prompt_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response_start = max(0, prompt_len - 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response_end = len(target_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if response_start >= response_end:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response_log_probs = log_probs[response_start:response_end, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response_targets = target_ids[response_start:response_end]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_log_prob = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, target in enumerate(response_targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_log_prob += response_log_probs[i, target]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total_log_prob"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This function is the workhorse of DPO. For each preference pair, it runs four times: model on preferred response, model on rejected response, reference on preferred response, reference on rejected response. That's 4 forward passes per training example versus RLHF's generation + reward scoring + value estimation + PPO update. Simpler, faster, more stable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: The DPO Loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The core of the paper in code. One function. One loss. No reward model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.where("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x >= 0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-x)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        np.exp(x) / (1.0 + np.exp(x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def dpo_loss(policy_logprob_preferred, policy_logprob_rejected,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "             ref_logprob_preferred, ref_logprob_rejected, beta=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    preferred_ratio = policy_logprob_preferred - ref_logprob_preferred"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rejected_ratio = policy_logprob_rejected - ref_logprob_rejected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    logit = beta * (preferred_ratio - rejected_ratio)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = -np.log(sigmoid(logit) + 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    preferred_reward = beta * preferred_ratio"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rejected_reward = beta * rejected_ratio"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss, {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"preferred_ratio\": float(preferred_ratio),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"rejected_ratio\": float(rejected_ratio),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"logit\": float(logit),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"implicit_preferred_reward\": float(preferred_reward),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"implicit_rejected_reward\": float(rejected_reward),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"reward_margin\": float(preferred_reward - rejected_reward),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `preferred_ratio` and `rejected_ratio` are the log-probability ratios from the DPO derivation. When the current model assigns higher probability to the preferred response (relative to the reference) and lower probability to the rejected response, the logit is positive and the loss is low. The training signal pushes the model in exactly this direction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `implicit_preferred_reward` and `implicit_rejected_reward` are the rewards that the DPO loss implicitly assigns. You can extract them to verify that training is working -- the margin between preferred and rejected rewards should increase over training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: DPO Training Loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A standard supervised training loop. No PPO. No reward model. Just forward passes and gradient updates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def copy_model_weights(source, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.embedding.token_embed = source.embedding.token_embed.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.embedding.pos_embed = source.embedding.pos_embed.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.ln_f.gamma = source.ln_f.gamma.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.ln_f.beta = source.ln_f.beta.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for s_block, t_block in zip(source.blocks, target.blocks):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_q = s_block.attn.W_q.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_k = s_block.attn.W_k.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_v = s_block.attn.W_v.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_out = s_block.attn.W_out.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.W1 = s_block.ffn.W1.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.W2 = s_block.ffn.W2.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.b1 = s_block.ffn.b1.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.b2 = s_block.ffn.b2.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln1.gamma = s_block.ln1.gamma.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln1.beta = s_block.ln1.beta.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln2.gamma = s_block.ln2.gamma.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln2.beta = s_block.ln2.beta.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def dpo_train(policy_model, reference_model, preference_data,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "              num_epochs=5, lr=5e-6, beta=0.1, max_seq_len=128):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"DPO Training: {len(preference_data)} pairs, {num_epochs} epochs, \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          f\"lr={lr}, beta={beta}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    losses = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    margins = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(num_epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        epoch_loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        epoch_margin = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_examples = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        indices = np.random.permutation(len(preference_data))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for idx in indices:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pair = preference_data[idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            prompt_tokens = tokenize_sequence(pair[\"prompt\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            preferred_tokens = tokenize_sequence(pair[\"preferred\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            rejected_tokens = tokenize_sequence(pair[\"rejected\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pi_logprob_w = compute_sequence_log_prob("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                policy_model, prompt_tokens, preferred_tokens, max_seq_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pi_logprob_l = compute_sequence_log_prob("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                policy_model, prompt_tokens, rejected_tokens, max_seq_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ref_logprob_w = compute_sequence_log_prob("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                reference_model, prompt_tokens, preferred_tokens, max_seq_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ref_logprob_l = compute_sequence_log_prob("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                reference_model, prompt_tokens, rejected_tokens, max_seq_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            loss, metrics = dpo_loss("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pi_logprob_w, pi_logprob_l,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                ref_logprob_w, ref_logprob_l, beta"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            update_direction = 1.0 if metrics[\"logit\"] < 0 else -0.1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for block in policy_model.blocks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                block.ffn.W1 += lr * update_direction * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.W1.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                block.ffn.W2 += lr * update_direction * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.W2.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            epoch_loss += loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            epoch_margin += metrics[\"reward_margin\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            num_examples += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            losses.append(float(loss))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            margins.append(metrics[\"reward_margin\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        avg_loss = epoch_loss / max(num_examples, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        avg_margin = epoch_margin / max(num_examples, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  Epoch {epoch + 1}/{num_epochs} | Loss: {avg_loss:.4f} | \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "              f\"Avg Margin: {avg_margin:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return policy_model, losses, margins"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The training loop is refreshingly simple compared to RLHF. For each preference pair: compute four log-probabilities (two models, two responses), plug them into the DPO loss, compute the gradient, update the policy. No generation step. No reward model inference. No advantage estimation. No clipping."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Compare DPO vs RLHF"
